        "mission_intent": "Team, we need a comprehensive collection requirement built out against PRC intelligence services' expanding use of AI-enabled surveillance and big data analytics for operations beyond China's borders, as highlighted in the latest annual threat assessment. The requirement should task SIGINT, OSINT, and HUMINT streams to identify specific PRC intelligence platforms and tools being adapted for extraterritorial political security targeting, including any indicators of technical collection infrastructure being positioned in or near allied nations. I want coverage of how PRC entities are leveraging the domestic surveillance ecosystem\u2014ubiquitous monitoring, bulk data acquisition\u2014and extending those capabilities internationally against perceived regime threats and for IP theft supporting indigenous S&T development. Include collection on whether sub-national PRC actors or provincial-level officials may be freelancing influence operations they believe align with Beijing's strategic objectives, even without direct tasking from MSS or PLA leadership. Ensure the requirement accounts for physical domain indicators as well, given lessons from the 2023 high-altitude balloon incident, and flag any novel platforms or delivery mechanisms for intelligence collection over U.S. or allied territory. Priority is urgent; I need the draft specification routed through the collection management authority for validation within ten business days, with nominated sources and feasibility assessments from each contributing discipline included.",
